    {
      "id": "3da37064e7e6ddd17d3838064f3ac3b45a3c2fa2",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1930606694,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The clang checks failed because it detects a recursive call in:\n```\ndissect_rtps\n  dissect_rtps_submessages  <---------\n    dissect_rtps_submessage_v2       |\n      dissect_SECURE                 |\n        dissect_rtps_submessages ----|\n```\nHowever, this makes sense because of what we are doing is: if the submessage is encrypted, then decrypt it, and call the dissect function again.\nThis recursion could be problematic if we had another pre-shared key encrypted submessage (in the one we just decrypted). This is not possible because we can only have pre-shared encryption at the RTPS message level; submessages are not encrypted using pre-shared keys. I added a `dissecting_encrypted_submessage` parameter that it is only true when we call `dissect_rtps_submessages` from `dissect_SECURE`. It makes sure that we never try to decrypt and parse the already decrypted and parsed submessage.",
          "author": {
            "id": 382912,
            "username": "colmenero",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Luis",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/382912/avatar.png?v=1787135174",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/colmenero"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-31T10:46:11.179Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-04T09:11:37.752Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 305490528,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
